1
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:05,500
[barking growl]

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:07,083
Excuse me,

3
00:00:07,083 --> 00:00:09,291
white, blue and pink
is where it's at.

4
00:00:09,291 --> 00:00:10,416
End of conversation.

5
00:00:10,416 --> 00:00:11,458
It's a good look,

6
00:00:11,458 --> 00:00:13,041
I'm not saying
it's not a good look.

7
00:00:13,041 --> 00:00:14,458
Mine's just cooler.

8
00:00:14,458 --> 00:00:15,458
That's subjective.

9
00:00:15,458 --> 00:00:16,375
Exactly.

10
00:00:16,375 --> 00:00:17,458
My Gi color

11
00:00:17,458 --> 00:00:18,833
is subjectively
cooler than yours.

12
00:00:18,833 --> 00:00:20,291
Do you even know
what "subjective" means--

13
00:00:20,291 --> 00:00:22,541
Will you two knock it off?

14
00:00:22,541 --> 00:00:23,833
Of course, Lloyd.

15
00:00:23,833 --> 00:00:25,666
Right after you confirm my Gi
is the coolest color scheme.

16
00:00:25,666 --> 00:00:29,000
I am not getting involved
in this.

17
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,791
Although everyone knows
green is the best.

18
00:00:30,791 --> 00:00:31,791
What was that?

19
00:00:31,791 --> 00:00:32,750
Nothing.

20
00:00:32,750 --> 00:00:34,041
Stay focused.

21
00:00:34,041 --> 00:00:36,083
It's getting harder and harder
to find the trail

22
00:00:36,083 --> 00:00:39,666
that Arin, and whoever
he's with, have left.

23
00:00:39,666 --> 00:00:41,916
What if he's stuck alone
with Ras?

24
00:00:41,916 --> 00:00:44,291
Ras is a master manipulator.

25
00:00:44,291 --> 00:00:46,041
He could be brainwashing Arin,

26
00:00:46,041 --> 00:00:47,666
and Arin would have no clue.

27
00:00:47,666 --> 00:00:49,916
It's getting dark,

28
00:00:49,916 --> 00:00:50,916
hard to see.

29
00:00:50,916 --> 00:00:52,416
We'd better stop and make camp.

30
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:57,000
[grumbling]

31
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,000
[barking]

32
00:01:01,583 --> 00:01:03,541
Did you know Arin's the one
who taught me

33
00:01:03,541 --> 00:01:04,916
how to make a campfire?

34
00:01:04,916 --> 00:01:05,833
Yeah.

35
00:01:05,833 --> 00:01:07,000
In Imperium,

36
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:08,541
all our heating
was turned on by a switch.

37
00:01:09,833 --> 00:01:11,041
[sighing heavily]

38
00:01:11,041 --> 00:01:13,708
I didn't know I could miss
a person this much.

39
00:01:13,708 --> 00:01:17,000
How does Zane deal with Pixal
being missing for so long?

40
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:18,375
Zane's a Nindroid.

41
00:01:18,375 --> 00:01:19,916
Can he even have emotions?

42
00:01:19,916 --> 00:01:21,125
[Lloyd laughing]

43
00:01:21,125 --> 00:01:24,291
Ah, you have a lot to learn
about Zane, Frak.

44
00:01:24,291 --> 00:01:26,916
He is much, much more
than a machine.

45
00:01:26,916 --> 00:01:28,333
I hope he's okay.

46
00:01:28,333 --> 00:01:30,000
We haven't heard from him
since we split up.

47
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,458
Maybe he's having
more success at finding Arin

48
00:01:32,458 --> 00:01:33,833
than we are?

49
00:01:35,916 --> 00:01:37,708
No significant signs of life--

50
00:01:37,708 --> 00:01:39,583
organic or otherwise.

51
00:01:39,583 --> 00:01:42,291
Let us move on
to the next valley.

52
00:01:42,291 --> 00:01:46,416
[bird chirping]

53
00:01:46,416 --> 00:01:49,375
[roaring in imitation]

54
00:01:49,375 --> 00:01:51,333
[chirping and singing]

55
00:01:55,458 --> 00:01:58,250
Do not dance with birds, Zanth.

56
00:01:58,250 --> 00:02:00,250
I once did such things,

57
00:02:00,250 --> 00:02:01,291
but have since learned

58
00:02:01,291 --> 00:02:03,041
that behavior
is considered weird.

59
00:02:03,041 --> 00:02:04,166
[groaning sadly]

60
00:02:06,625 --> 00:02:08,208
[bird singing]

61
00:02:12,125 --> 00:02:14,750
This area looks
as empty as the others.

62
00:02:20,708 --> 00:02:23,041
Could that be
what I think it is?

63
00:02:25,625 --> 00:02:28,750
♪ Lost in the unknown ♪

64
00:02:28,750 --> 00:02:31,833
♪ Together we will rise ♪

65
00:02:31,833 --> 00:02:34,250
♪ We fight ♪

66
00:02:34,250 --> 00:02:38,416
♪ Be a ninja
for what's right ♪♪

67
00:02:47,416 --> 00:02:48,791
This is like
the other Monasteries

68
00:02:48,791 --> 00:02:50,458
we have discovered.

69
00:02:50,458 --> 00:02:53,500
Similar to ours,
yet strangely different.

70
00:02:55,916 --> 00:02:57,250
[sniffing]

71
00:02:57,250 --> 00:03:00,000
If my theory that each realm
gained its own Monastery

72
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:01,083
during the Merge

73
00:03:01,083 --> 00:03:02,166
is true,

74
00:03:02,166 --> 00:03:04,416
then this must be
this land's Monastery.

75
00:03:07,875 --> 00:03:09,041
Hello?

76
00:03:09,041 --> 00:03:10,291
Is anyone here?

77
00:03:11,208 --> 00:03:12,416
A portal gate!

78
00:03:12,416 --> 00:03:14,833
Exactly like
the other Monasteries.

79
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:22,708
[voices approaching]

80
00:03:24,125 --> 00:03:25,250
Come on, Rapton!

81
00:03:25,250 --> 00:03:26,833
This would be
a whole lot easier

82
00:03:26,833 --> 00:03:28,041
if you'd just let us use a cart!

83
00:03:29,208 --> 00:03:30,416
No way,

84
00:03:30,416 --> 00:03:32,583
carts are Rapton's nemesis!

85
00:03:32,583 --> 00:03:33,875
They know what they did.

86
00:03:33,875 --> 00:03:36,833
Ah, besides, a little hard work
never hurt anybody.

87
00:03:36,833 --> 00:03:39,625
Clearly, you've already
forgotten about Richard,

88
00:03:39,625 --> 00:03:41,000
and statistically,

89
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,208
hard work
is the leading cause of--

90
00:03:42,208 --> 00:03:43,500
It's about to become

91
00:03:43,500 --> 00:03:45,291
the leading cause
of my boot in--

92
00:03:45,291 --> 00:03:47,166
Um...

93
00:03:47,166 --> 00:03:48,625
Excuse me, Rapton.

94
00:03:48,625 --> 00:03:50,875
I do not believe those items
belong to you

95
00:03:50,875 --> 00:03:52,083
or the Freebooters.

96
00:03:52,083 --> 00:03:55,416
Oh, great, the ice cream ninja.

97
00:03:55,416 --> 00:03:58,083
Uh, we have paperwork,
Mr. Ninja,

98
00:03:58,083 --> 00:03:59,833
from a... dude.

99
00:03:59,833 --> 00:04:02,000
The chain of ownership
is kinda murky, but--

100
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:04,125
Will you let Rapton
do the talking?

101
00:04:04,125 --> 00:04:06,041
Just blast him!

102
00:04:10,916 --> 00:04:13,041
Don't drop any of that stuff!

103
00:04:13,041 --> 00:04:15,541
Please don't question
our professionalism.

104
00:04:15,541 --> 00:04:17,625
We're very good looters.

105
00:04:17,625 --> 00:04:20,625
Oh, so then
you don't need a cart!

106
00:04:20,625 --> 00:04:23,583
Ugh!
Foiled by my own logic!

107
00:04:36,625 --> 00:04:37,625
It cannot be!

108
00:04:42,708 --> 00:04:44,291
[door crumbling]

109
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:56,250
No!

110
00:04:58,625 --> 00:05:00,583
Excellent timing, Zanth!

111
00:05:02,291 --> 00:05:03,708
Try to get me closer!

112
00:05:13,291 --> 00:05:15,416
Almost...

113
00:05:15,416 --> 00:05:16,916
[grunting with effort]

114
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:25,083
No life forms inside...

115
00:05:25,083 --> 00:05:26,125
there!

116
00:05:26,125 --> 00:05:28,583
Just what I was looking for!

117
00:05:32,416 --> 00:05:34,000
[gasping]

118
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:35,000
[rock slamming]

119
00:05:40,041 --> 00:05:41,875
Kreel would be jealous.

120
00:05:41,875 --> 00:05:44,000
It is a literal junkyard
in here.

121
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:46,625
The Freebooters have been
more successful at looting

122
00:05:46,625 --> 00:05:48,125
than I would have imagined,

123
00:05:48,125 --> 00:05:49,625
but where...

124
00:05:49,625 --> 00:05:50,541
A-ha!

125
00:05:58,500 --> 00:06:01,625
If Kai and Nya could open
the Cocoon I was found in,

126
00:06:01,625 --> 00:06:05,375
surely I can find a way
to open this one.

127
00:06:11,041 --> 00:06:13,333
[mechanism powering on]

128
00:06:15,791 --> 00:06:16,833
[hissing open]

129
00:06:20,708 --> 00:06:24,833
Primary Interactive X-ternal
Assistant Life-Form now online.

130
00:06:24,833 --> 00:06:25,833
Pixal!

131
00:06:28,541 --> 00:06:30,083
Zane?

132
00:06:38,541 --> 00:06:41,791
[sighing] Can't he ever come
at a normal hour?

133
00:06:41,791 --> 00:06:42,750
Guess when you're him,

134
00:06:42,750 --> 00:06:44,458
you show up whenever you want.

135
00:06:44,458 --> 00:06:47,125
Just wish he'd stop
poking holes in my door.

136
00:06:53,750 --> 00:06:56,416
A successful mission?

137
00:06:56,416 --> 00:06:58,916
I never fail.

138
00:06:58,916 --> 00:07:00,000
May I see it?

139
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:01,333
Money first.

140
00:07:01,333 --> 00:07:03,250
Oh, of course.

141
00:07:06,791 --> 00:07:08,416
Congratulations.

142
00:07:08,416 --> 00:07:11,208
You just bought yourself
a rare Oni chalice

143
00:07:11,208 --> 00:07:12,583
from the First Realm.

144
00:07:12,583 --> 00:07:13,791
[hissing in delight]

145
00:07:13,791 --> 00:07:15,083
I never dreamed

146
00:07:15,083 --> 00:07:17,375
I'd get my hands
on such a thing.

147
00:07:17,375 --> 00:07:18,625
Glorious!

148
00:07:18,625 --> 00:07:21,000
Then our transaction
is complete.

149
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:22,250
Wait.

150
00:07:22,250 --> 00:07:25,083
I was asked to pass
a message on to you.

151
00:07:25,083 --> 00:07:28,625
Someone else
wants to contract your services.

152
00:07:30,500 --> 00:07:32,291
Who is this from?

153
00:07:32,291 --> 00:07:33,333
I don't know.

154
00:07:33,333 --> 00:07:35,416
They were very secretive.

155
00:07:35,416 --> 00:07:37,750
Asked you to meet them
at that location

156
00:07:37,750 --> 00:07:40,125
in two days' time.

157
00:07:45,333 --> 00:07:47,708
[Zane] I was beginning to fear
I would never see you again!

158
00:07:47,708 --> 00:07:50,125
[Pixal]
I do not understand, Zane.

159
00:07:50,125 --> 00:07:51,625
Why are you acting like this?

160
00:07:52,666 --> 00:07:55,541
We just saw each other
this morning.

161
00:07:55,541 --> 00:07:59,250
Though I am not sure
how I got in this weird place.

162
00:07:59,250 --> 00:08:01,750
What is the last thing
you remember?

163
00:08:01,750 --> 00:08:03,875
Some kind of strange storm.

164
00:08:03,875 --> 00:08:05,666
Then everything went dark,

165
00:08:05,666 --> 00:08:09,000
and now, you're
letting me out of this... thing.

166
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:10,833
Pixal,

167
00:08:10,833 --> 00:08:13,500
it has been years
since we have seen each other.

168
00:08:13,500 --> 00:08:14,833
The storm you remember

169
00:08:14,833 --> 00:08:17,125
is something we now call
"the Merge,"

170
00:08:17,125 --> 00:08:18,291
a mysterious event

171
00:08:18,291 --> 00:08:20,958
that combined all the realms
into one,

172
00:08:20,958 --> 00:08:23,666
apparently orchestrated
by Master Wu.

173
00:08:24,666 --> 00:08:26,333
Master Wu?

174
00:08:26,333 --> 00:08:27,333
Is he here as well?

175
00:08:29,500 --> 00:08:32,708
It is very likely
he has departed.

176
00:08:32,708 --> 00:08:36,125
Many strange things
have happened since the Merge.

177
00:08:36,125 --> 00:08:38,583
I woke up
in a similar techno-cocoon

178
00:08:38,583 --> 00:08:41,416
inside another Monastery
we found.

179
00:08:41,416 --> 00:08:42,958
I will have to investigate

180
00:08:42,958 --> 00:08:44,583
why that would happen
to us both.

181
00:08:44,583 --> 00:08:46,708
There are other Monasteries?

182
00:08:46,708 --> 00:08:49,041
There are also new Ninja!

183
00:08:49,041 --> 00:08:50,166
[imitating Arin's voice]
Like Arin!

184
00:08:50,166 --> 00:08:52,250
He's self-taught
in the art of Spinjitzu...

185
00:08:54,291 --> 00:08:55,833
...and the art of making pies!

186
00:08:56,833 --> 00:08:58,250
[imitating Sora's voice]
And Sora!

187
00:08:58,250 --> 00:09:00,916
A master
at elemental tech abilities.

188
00:09:00,916 --> 00:09:03,375
Not sure about her pie-making
abilities, however.

189
00:09:03,375 --> 00:09:05,208
[in his own voice]
Then there's Riyu!

190
00:09:05,208 --> 00:09:08,333
He is a small dragon
and doesn't talk like this.

191
00:09:08,333 --> 00:09:10,125
He mostly makes sounds like--

192
00:09:10,125 --> 00:09:13,125
[croaking and barking]

193
00:09:13,125 --> 00:09:14,500
[snorting snarl]

194
00:09:14,500 --> 00:09:17,208
[imitating Wyldfyre's voice]
Oh, and I can't forget Wyldfyre!

195
00:09:17,208 --> 00:09:19,458
she would be upset
she wasn't mentioned first.

196
00:09:19,458 --> 00:09:21,208
She's fiery,

197
00:09:21,208 --> 00:09:22,333
but not Kai-fiery.

198
00:09:22,333 --> 00:09:23,333
It was a thing.

199
00:09:23,333 --> 00:09:25,708
I'm sad
to have missed all that.

200
00:09:25,708 --> 00:09:29,583
[in his own voice]
I am sad you have as well.

201
00:09:29,583 --> 00:09:32,291
During my most dire times
since the Merge,

202
00:09:32,291 --> 00:09:34,291
when I was losing hope,

203
00:09:34,291 --> 00:09:37,291
I would hear a voice in my head.

204
00:09:37,291 --> 00:09:39,166
A voice that would center me,

205
00:09:39,166 --> 00:09:41,166
giving me drive to continue,

206
00:09:41,166 --> 00:09:44,500
even when the odds
were increasingly against us.

207
00:09:48,541 --> 00:09:51,291
That voice, Pixal, was yours.

208
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:55,208
[Rapton] Aw...

209
00:09:57,583 --> 00:10:01,291
Hate to break up
this tender moment...

210
00:10:01,291 --> 00:10:05,333
Ha! Nah, Rapton loves
ruining tender moments!

211
00:10:05,333 --> 00:10:07,833
That's an odd thing
to be in love with.

212
00:10:07,833 --> 00:10:10,125
I was being
rhetorically dramatic!

213
00:10:10,125 --> 00:10:11,750
You really should watch
more theater!

214
00:10:13,500 --> 00:10:16,375
Hey, Ninja,
that robot is our loot,

215
00:10:16,375 --> 00:10:18,375
and we hate losing our loot!

216
00:10:18,375 --> 00:10:21,208
So either you voluntarily
cage yourselves,

217
00:10:21,208 --> 00:10:24,416
or we're gonna have to turn
you both into scrap.

218
00:10:26,750 --> 00:10:28,625
Shall we do what we do best?

219
00:10:28,625 --> 00:10:30,000
I have missed you.

220
00:10:31,666 --> 00:10:32,708
[grunting with effort]

221
00:10:34,666 --> 00:10:36,500
Ah... h'yah!

222
00:10:48,083 --> 00:10:49,291
Look out!

223
00:10:54,416 --> 00:10:55,458
Ah!

224
00:10:58,000 --> 00:10:58,958
R'ah!

225
00:10:58,958 --> 00:11:00,583
[grunting with effort]

226
00:11:06,416 --> 00:11:07,500
[blasting]

227
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:10,125
[grunting with effort]

228
00:11:10,125 --> 00:11:11,208
[gasping]

229
00:11:17,958 --> 00:11:18,791
H'ah!

230
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:22,083
Incoming!

231
00:11:22,083 --> 00:11:23,375
Understood.

232
00:11:23,375 --> 00:11:24,666
[grunting with effort]

233
00:11:28,791 --> 00:11:30,416
H'ah!

234
00:11:30,416 --> 00:11:31,875
[grunting]

235
00:11:33,083 --> 00:11:34,000
[grunting] Unh!

236
00:11:35,458 --> 00:11:37,166
I love the other Ninja,

237
00:11:37,166 --> 00:11:39,958
but you are the only one
who thinks the way I do, Pixal.

238
00:11:39,958 --> 00:11:42,958
I am a bit surprised
to hear you so emotional.

239
00:11:43,916 --> 00:11:47,041
It has been
a long time for me.

240
00:11:51,583 --> 00:11:52,791
We have 'em!

241
00:11:52,791 --> 00:11:55,500
How exactly do we have them?

242
00:11:55,500 --> 00:11:58,333
Ah, well, we will have them
very shortly.

243
00:11:58,333 --> 00:12:00,791
Appreciate the clarification.

244
00:12:05,500 --> 00:12:08,625
We appear to be pinned down.

245
00:12:08,625 --> 00:12:11,166
Appearances can be deceiving.

246
00:12:11,166 --> 00:12:12,708
We simply need to leave,

247
00:12:12,708 --> 00:12:14,583
in classic Ninja style.

248
00:12:17,458 --> 00:12:19,208
[coughing]

249
00:12:19,208 --> 00:12:20,208
Wh-What?

250
00:12:20,208 --> 00:12:21,416
Is that a campfire?

251
00:12:21,416 --> 00:12:22,416
[coughing]

252
00:12:26,083 --> 00:12:27,166
There!

253
00:12:28,500 --> 00:12:29,500
It's locked!

254
00:12:32,166 --> 00:12:34,125
[Rapton] Get it open!

255
00:12:34,125 --> 00:12:36,666
We need a safe spot to leap!

256
00:12:38,916 --> 00:12:41,916
Somewhere we won't
get crushed against a rock.

257
00:12:41,916 --> 00:12:43,041
That also.

258
00:12:43,041 --> 00:12:44,000
Up ahead!

259
00:12:45,625 --> 00:12:47,250
Get ready to jump!

260
00:12:47,250 --> 00:12:49,333
One, two...

261
00:12:49,333 --> 00:12:50,833
[thunderclaps]

262
00:12:50,833 --> 00:12:52,375
Is that lightning?

263
00:12:59,416 --> 00:13:01,166
This is very bad.

264
00:13:01,166 --> 00:13:02,250
You know them?

265
00:13:02,250 --> 00:13:04,000
I know the one in front.

266
00:13:08,166 --> 00:13:10,666
And he'll probably tell us
something like--

267
00:13:10,666 --> 00:13:13,958
[imitating Nokt's voice]
I will crush you to your doom.

268
00:13:13,958 --> 00:13:15,750
Come, Dragonians!

269
00:13:15,750 --> 00:13:18,958
Let us crush them
to their doom!

270
00:13:19,916 --> 00:13:22,916
Sometimes,
I hate being so accurate.

271
00:13:24,666 --> 00:13:26,708
Nokt is most likely
coming for me.

272
00:13:26,708 --> 00:13:28,583
We must get off this train

273
00:13:28,583 --> 00:13:30,458
and get as far away as possible.

274
00:13:30,458 --> 00:13:33,083
On the count of three, we jump.

275
00:13:33,083 --> 00:13:34,041
One--

276
00:13:34,041 --> 00:13:35,375
[Nokt] We don't leave here

277
00:13:35,375 --> 00:13:36,916
without the blade!

278
00:13:39,583 --> 00:13:42,958
[Nokt]
No one onboard remains alive!

279
00:13:42,958 --> 00:13:45,375
So Nokt is here
for some other reason.

280
00:13:45,375 --> 00:13:47,750
I hate when
I am inaccurate as well.

281
00:13:47,750 --> 00:13:50,083
He wants some sort of blade?

282
00:13:50,083 --> 00:13:52,583
So we continue
doing what we do best.

283
00:14:05,375 --> 00:14:06,375
[yelping]

284
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:10,958
[grunting with effort]

285
00:14:10,958 --> 00:14:12,625
Who are these people now?

286
00:14:13,625 --> 00:14:16,041
Can't anyone just loot
in peace anymore?

287
00:14:16,041 --> 00:14:18,875
[blasting]

288
00:14:28,791 --> 00:14:31,625
[growling]

289
00:14:31,625 --> 00:14:35,000
It has to be here somewhere!

290
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:36,750
[gasping]

291
00:14:38,166 --> 00:14:40,583
Finally.

292
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:44,416
H'yah!

293
00:14:44,416 --> 00:14:45,500
What?

294
00:14:48,166 --> 00:14:50,208
You!

295
00:14:50,208 --> 00:14:53,625
I'd been hoping for a rematch
with the Ninja.

296
00:14:55,416 --> 00:14:58,166
I have recently seen
another blade like this.

297
00:14:58,166 --> 00:15:01,000
Its kind of power
should not be in your hands!

298
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:03,791
I don't care what you think.

299
00:15:03,791 --> 00:15:05,916
[roaring]

300
00:15:11,500 --> 00:15:13,375
[Nokt growling]

301
00:15:13,375 --> 00:15:14,958
[grunting with effort]

302
00:15:14,958 --> 00:15:16,583
[snarling]

303
00:15:18,416 --> 00:15:21,166
[Freebooters shouting]

304
00:15:23,333 --> 00:15:25,375
H'ah!

305
00:15:25,375 --> 00:15:26,583
[blades clanking]

306
00:15:28,458 --> 00:15:30,833
Um, are we on the same side?

307
00:15:30,833 --> 00:15:33,000
-For now.
-Oh, thank goodness.

308
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:35,291
I couldn't handle
being kicked by more people.

309
00:15:37,750 --> 00:15:38,666
H'ah!

310
00:15:44,500 --> 00:15:47,208
[snarling]

311
00:15:55,125 --> 00:15:56,291
H'ah!

312
00:15:57,291 --> 00:15:59,208
[grunting with effort]

313
00:16:01,916 --> 00:16:03,708
Give me that blade!

314
00:16:03,708 --> 00:16:05,375
[roaring] Y'ah! H'ah!

315
00:16:07,208 --> 00:16:09,166
[blasting]

316
00:16:15,375 --> 00:16:16,375
H'ah!

317
00:16:17,208 --> 00:16:18,125
H'ah!

318
00:16:21,583 --> 00:16:22,583
H'ah!

319
00:16:26,500 --> 00:16:27,958
[grunting with effort]

320
00:16:33,375 --> 00:16:35,125
Bring me that sword!

321
00:16:51,208 --> 00:16:52,666
[cackling]

322
00:16:57,875 --> 00:16:59,541
After her!

323
00:17:07,166 --> 00:17:08,458
Ah! Whoa!

324
00:17:08,458 --> 00:17:09,500
[grunting with effort]

325
00:17:12,916 --> 00:17:13,875
H'ah!

326
00:17:18,916 --> 00:17:20,166
[grunting with effort]

327
00:17:21,458 --> 00:17:23,000
Unh! Ah!

328
00:17:26,375 --> 00:17:27,666
Ah! Oh!

329
00:17:27,666 --> 00:17:29,458
[gasping]

330
00:17:31,083 --> 00:17:32,041
Yes!

331
00:17:36,166 --> 00:17:37,208
No!

332
00:17:40,416 --> 00:17:41,958
H'ah!

333
00:17:44,208 --> 00:17:45,125
[snarling]

334
00:17:47,541 --> 00:17:48,458
[grunting with effort]

335
00:17:53,666 --> 00:17:54,958
Forget the ninja,

336
00:17:54,958 --> 00:17:57,583
the weak point is the train.

337
00:18:03,083 --> 00:18:05,583
[grunting with effort]

338
00:18:06,916 --> 00:18:08,375
[train power surging]

339
00:18:10,916 --> 00:18:12,791
[gasping]

340
00:18:15,875 --> 00:18:19,083
It was nice to see you again.

341
00:18:21,041 --> 00:18:23,375
[gasping]

342
00:18:23,375 --> 00:18:24,541
Ah!

343
00:18:25,583 --> 00:18:26,875
Zane!

344
00:18:26,875 --> 00:18:28,791
The train is going faster!

345
00:18:28,791 --> 00:18:29,833
We're going to crash!

346
00:18:30,666 --> 00:18:32,416
Nokt is escaping,

347
00:18:32,416 --> 00:18:35,000
and there is no way
to get the fallen Freebooters

348
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,125
safely off the train.

349
00:18:36,125 --> 00:18:37,625
[Pixal]
And we are about to crash.

350
00:18:37,625 --> 00:18:39,125
Don't forget the crash!

351
00:18:39,125 --> 00:18:42,625
[Zane] I must find a way
to override the train controls!

352
00:18:42,625 --> 00:18:43,708
[Pixal] Manually?

353
00:18:43,708 --> 00:18:45,250
But the chances of success are--

354
00:18:45,250 --> 00:18:48,041
[Zane] I am well aware
of my slim chances.

355
00:18:48,041 --> 00:18:49,916
[Pixal] Of course you are.

356
00:18:53,791 --> 00:18:55,916
Whoa!

357
00:18:55,916 --> 00:18:57,625
[grunting with effort]

358
00:18:57,625 --> 00:18:59,083
Ah!

359
00:19:00,208 --> 00:19:02,416
This should work.

360
00:19:02,416 --> 00:19:03,541
[grunting with effort]

361
00:19:04,833 --> 00:19:07,125
I was presumptuous.

362
00:19:08,791 --> 00:19:12,333
And we are out of time.

363
00:19:14,750 --> 00:19:16,083
Zane! No!

364
00:19:17,125 --> 00:19:18,375
[electricity crackling,
Zane groaning in pain]

365
00:19:19,541 --> 00:19:20,958
[screaming]

366
00:19:27,791 --> 00:19:29,083
[brakes screeching]

367
00:19:32,041 --> 00:19:34,833
[screaming and groaning]

368
00:19:34,833 --> 00:19:37,208
[brakes grinding]

369
00:19:46,208 --> 00:19:48,250
[chuckling in triumph]

370
00:19:48,250 --> 00:19:52,666
Rapton saves us yet again!

371
00:19:52,666 --> 00:19:55,416
I was... not sure.

372
00:19:55,416 --> 00:19:56,375
[groaning in pain]

373
00:19:57,541 --> 00:20:00,333
[gasping]

374
00:20:00,333 --> 00:20:01,916
Zane!

375
00:20:03,625 --> 00:20:04,750
[electricity crackling]

376
00:20:04,750 --> 00:20:06,333
Zane, no!

377
00:20:06,333 --> 00:20:07,333
Listen to me!

378
00:20:07,333 --> 00:20:09,125
It's Pixal, hear my voice!

379
00:20:09,125 --> 00:20:11,208
[electricity crackling]

380
00:20:11,208 --> 00:20:12,208
Zane!

381
00:20:12,208 --> 00:20:13,208
Come back to me!

382
00:20:13,208 --> 00:20:15,083
Pixal...

383
00:20:15,083 --> 00:20:16,625
I thought I'd... lost you...

384
00:20:16,625 --> 00:20:18,416
Never again.

385
00:20:18,416 --> 00:20:20,125
[groaning in pain]

386
00:20:20,125 --> 00:20:21,625
You're seriously damaged.

387
00:20:21,625 --> 00:20:24,000
We need to get you help,
quickly.

388
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:25,083
We have...

389
00:20:25,083 --> 00:20:26,541
other problems.

390
00:20:26,541 --> 00:20:28,083
The Forbidden Five...

391
00:20:28,083 --> 00:20:30,750
must be stopped.

392
00:20:42,375 --> 00:20:43,375
[gasping]

393
00:20:43,375 --> 00:20:44,625
[thunderclaps]

394
00:20:48,583 --> 00:20:50,208
[snarling]

395
00:20:50,208 --> 00:20:51,875
[screaming]

396
00:21:27,041 --> 00:21:28,125
[shattering stone]

397
00:21:34,916 --> 00:21:35,833
Hmm...

398
00:21:35,833 --> 00:21:39,625
Exactly what we came for.

399
00:21:39,625 --> 00:21:41,916
[evil laughter]

400
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:46,791
[♪♪♪]

